# DENTAL-CHART-ASSET-R3 - generated tooth SVG assets.
#
# These 104 files are written by `npm run assets:teeth` and guarded by a
# byte-for-byte drift test (scripts/dental-assets/__tests__). The exporter
# emits LF, and today the committed blobs are LF, so the guard passes on both
# a Windows author machine and the ubuntu CI runner.
#
# That currently holds only because every author so far has core.autocrlf=true,
# which normalises on commit. It is not a property of the repository. A
# contributor with autocrlf=false on Windows would commit CRLF blobs; ubuntu
# CI would check those bytes out verbatim; and the drift guard would compare a
# CRLF file against LF-generated content and fail. The failure reproduces on
# Linux only and reads as "stale assets", pointing the next person at the
# exporter instead of at line endings.
#
# Pinning blob and working copy to LF makes the generated bytes identical on
# every platform regardless of local git config - which is the property the
# drift guard assumes.
design/dental-chart/final-svg/** text eol=lf
